Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 15:34:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] S306p a heartbeat while cards wait on seats (the framework's
 thin path; P-885; main's M84): the round's last line counts the cards that
 wait on a seat (OFFERED, AT_BANKING); a round that moved nothing and left
 nothing while one waits says the next round comes after a wait, and the job
 next waits 20 minutes and dispatches; the chain ends only when no card waits
 on anything a round can see; tests of the three cases, each rule taken out
 failing one

---
 .github/workflows/intake.yml   | 12 ++++++++--
 CHANGELOG.md                   | 10 ++++++++
 PROGRESS_LOG.md                |  8 +++++++
 docs/views/CONTEXT_RECOVERY.md |  2 +-
 queue/README.md                |  5 ++++
 scripts/queue/intake.py        | 16 +++++++++----
 tests/test_queue_intake.py     | 42 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 7 files changed, 86 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/intake.yml b/.github/workflows/intake.yml
index 6c17694c7..4b8cade0b 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/intake.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/intake.yml
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@
     timeout-minutes: 120
     outputs:
       again: ${{ steps.intake.outputs.again }}       # main's M83: the round's last line, read by the job `next`
+      wait: ${{ steps.intake.outputs.wait }}         # main's M84: cards wait on a seat and nothing moved
     steps:
       - name: Check out main, with every branch's history
         uses: actions/checkout@v4
@@ -78,6 +79,7 @@
             exit 1
           fi
           if grep -q "^the next round: needed" round_report.txt; then echo "again=true" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"; else echo "again=false" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"; fi
+          if grep -q "^the next round: after a wait" round_report.txt; then echo "wait=true" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"; else echo "wait=false" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"; fi
       - uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
         with:
           name: queue
@@ -159,13 +161,19 @@
     # no checkout, no seat code. It runs after the round was recorded, and only when the round's last line says the next
     # round is needed; a round with nothing to do ends the chain, and the hourly cron stays as the fallback. The
     # concurrency group above keeps one round at a time: the dispatched round waits until this one ends.
+    # CHANGED 2026-11-28 (main's M84 point 2): it also runs when the round moved nothing but cards wait on a seat (OFFERED,
+    # AT_BANKING), and then waits 20 minutes before it dispatches, so a seat's push is seen without the author's click.
+    # The lines as they stood: if: ${{ needs.round.outputs.again == 'true' }} and timeout-minutes: 5.
     needs: [round, record]
-    if: ${{ needs.round.outputs.again == 'true' }}
+    if: ${{ needs.round.outputs.again == 'true' || needs.round.outputs.wait == 'true' }}
     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
-    timeout-minutes: 5
+    timeout-minutes: 25
     permissions:
       actions: write                 # to dispatch the next round, with the job's own token; nothing else
     steps:
+      - name: Wait for the seats
+        if: ${{ needs.round.outputs.again != 'true' && needs.round.outputs.wait == 'true' }}
+        run: sleep 1200
       - name: Dispatch the next round
         env:
           GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}
